    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d5124649-7b95-50c9-8083-74c1e47c705b",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "Express $6\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{11\\pi}{12}\\right)-3$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&6\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{11\\pi}{12}\\right)-3\\\\&=3\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{11\\pi}{12}\\right)-1\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the alternative cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n2\\cos^2 x-1=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=\\frac{11\\pi}{12}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{11\\pi}{12}\\right)-1&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot \\frac{11\\pi}{12}\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(\\frac{11\\pi}{6}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3\\left(2\\cos^2\\left(\\frac{11\\pi}{12}\\right)-1\\right)&=3\\cos\\left(\\frac{11\\pi}{6}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
